{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Deadly hunger.</b> Those consumed by hunger — like the expression למזי לאתונא." "<b>And my weapons [of Reshef].</b> Birds of prey — as in 'go, my weapons, בלחמי'; and 'the sons of Reshef fly aloft' — עוף. Another interpretation: <b>and my weapons</b> — arrows, as in 'there He shattered the strings of my bow.' Another interpretation: <b>and my weapons</b> — fire of the enemies, as in 'her sparks רשפי אש.'" "<b>And the tooth of beast.</b> Wild beasts, for we find that a חיה is called בהמה, as in 'and the kite and every beast of the earth upon him shall brood.'" "<b>[I will send].b> Here it is written with a heavy paradigm and dagesh, because it is a dispatch of destruction."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {3 "The bracketed lemma in the source appears to enclose אשלח but the comment addresses the form אשלח as written in some textual tradition; rendered hyper-literally as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:12.177370781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}